  "street_name": "Surbiton Crescent",
  "decision_date": "09/10/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, due to the failure to achieve the minimum floor-to-ceiling height and poor layout of the ground floor flat, would provide a poor standard of accommodation for future occupants, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DM10 and DM13 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012).",
    "The proposed development, due to the loss of the sole window servicing the dining room and loss of the garden area for no.6 Surbiton Crescent, would result in unacceptable impacts on neighbouring occupants in terms of acccess to daylight and sunlight and loss of outdoor amenity space, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM10 and DM13 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), and Policy Guidance 13 of the RBK Residential Design SPD.",
    "The proposed development, as a result of no Unilateral Undertaking being secured to prevent future occupiers from applying for resident parking permits in the Controlled Parking Zone, would result in unacceptable impacts on highway function and safety, contrary to Paragraph 116 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy T4 and T6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies DM9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient information, in the form of a comprehensive Biodiversity Net Gain Assessment, has been submitted to determine a 10% BNG cannot be achieved on-site, contrary to Paragraph 193 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy G6 of the London Plan 2021, and Policy DM6 of the Core Strategy 2012.\r\r"
  ],
